<https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000064> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "People with aphallia have XY chromosomes, testes, and are born without a penis. They produce typical levels of testosterone, and they develop secondary sex characteristics associated with a typical testosterone puberty during adolescence."@en .
