<https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0002151> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Japanese word that means \"beautiful boy\" and is used to describe a particular aesthetic of androgynous male beauty. While in Japanese \"bishounen\" refers specifically to youths under the age of twenty and \"biseinen\" is used to describe beautiful adult men, English-speaking anime and manga fan communities often use \"bishounen\" in reference to any good-looking male character, regardless of age."@en .
