<https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003614> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://homosaurus.org/v3> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003615> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "homoit0003615" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003615> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Queer ecology"@en .
<https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003615> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Queer ecologies"@en .
<https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003615> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A school of ecology that seeks to understand nature, biology, and sexuality through the framing of queer theory. Queer ecology rejects the presumption of heterosexuality and cisgenderedness as natural, as well as notions of human exceptionalism and anthropocentrism."@en .
<https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003615> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001219> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003615> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#hasTopConcept> <https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0001365> .
