<https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003656> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch> <http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2016000166> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003656> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#hasTopConcept> <https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000861> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003656> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2024-10-22"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003656> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2025-01-26"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003656> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003656> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://homosaurus.org/v3> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003657> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "homoit0003657" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003657> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Gender-affirming care"@en .
<https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003657> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Gender affirming care"@en .
<https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003657> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Social, psychological, behavioral, and medical interventions designed to support and affirm an individual's gender identity. Gender-affirming care includes but is not limited to equal access to health care facilities, counseling, puberty blockers, hormone therapy, and gender-affirming surgeries. It can also include resources to aid in social transition, such as affirming policies regarding name and pronoun changes, access to non-gendered restrooms and facilities, etc."@en .
<https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0003657> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://homosaurus.org/v3/homoit0000614> .
